{
  "_meta": {
    "notes": "The career's only hiring surface. rp1.personnel.assign moves staff already on the books and deliberately buys none; the standing hire instruction is the command that spends. Nothing is charged at the press: HireStaffProject.IncrementProgress hires min(applicants + (funds - reserve) / perHire, left) every tick, so a career that cannot pay for the whole target hires what it can and comes back for the rest. A short balance SLOWS it and never refuses it, which is why the line beside the press is a BOUND on the spend and not an affordability verdict, and the bound is the operator's own reserve. RP-1 keeps one staffTarget per career and stores no field for the kind, only whether a complex is named, so this is one control and the picker sends lcId or omits it."
  },
